## Hard-won gotchas
- CLI `rpc submit-transaction` is **commented out / unsupported** — cannot submit
  via the wallet CLI. Network submission needs a wRPC client program; `rothschild`
  (in tree, already has tokio+wRPC) is the likely base.
- The VS Code **integrated terminal reverses multi-line pastes** line-by-line.
  Use single-line commands, or paste multi-line file contents into the VS Code
  **editor** (not terminal). Copy-an-existing-file + `-replace` works reliably.
- `silverc` constructor args are typed `Expr` JSON: int = `{"kind":"int","data":N}`,
  a `byte[8]` = an `array` of eight `{"kind":"byte","data":N}` (little-endian).
- Coinbase must mature (~100 confs) before spendable; `list` shows total incl.
  pending, `sweep`/`send` only use mature UTXOs.
- Kaspa ints in script are little-endian; `byte[8](100)` => `64 00 00 00 00 00 00 00`.
